The `updateAAD` method is used in the Authenticated Encryption with Associated Data (AEAD) Galois/Counter Mode (GCM) cipher algorithm for providing additional data, called Associated Data (AD), that needs to be authenticated along with the message being encrypted or decrypted. Here's how you can use it:

1. First, create an instance of the GCM cipher class and initialize it with your desired key and initialization vector (IV). For example:

```java
import javax.crypto.spec.GCMParameterSpec;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;

import com.google.crypto.tink.aead.Aes128Gcm;
import com.google.crypto.tink.aead.TinkAead;

public class GcmCipher {
    private final TinkAead gcm;

    public GcmCipher(byte[] key, byte[] iv) throws Exception {
        GCMParameterSpec spec = GCMParameterSpec.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding", 128);
        spec.setTLength(128);
        gcm = new Aes128Gcm(new SecretKeySpec(key, "AES"));
        gcm.init(true, spec.initialize(iv));
    }
}
```

2. Now, when you want to encrypt or decrypt a message with AD, call the `updateAAD` method before calling the encryption or decryption methods. Pass the AD as a byte array to this method.

```java
byte[] ad = ... // The associated data
byte[] message = ... // The message to be encrypted/decrypted
byte[] ciphertext = null;
byte[] plaintext = null;

try {
    gcm.updateAAD(ad);

    // Encryption
    ciphertext = gcm.encrypt(message);

    // Decryption
    plaintext = gcm.decrypt(ciphertext);
} catch (Exception e) {
    // Handle errors here
}
```

